{
  "name": "Monthly OPM hours and activity-driver surveys",
  "today": "Each month the Operations Pricing Model (OPM) team emails two surveys to operations managers: an hours survey (to about 50-57 managers) asking how their team's hours split across activities, and an activity-driver survey (to about 24-26 managers) asking for counts such as deals for each cost center (RC). Managers fill them in by hand and send them back. Many reply late, so the OPM team and senior managers send reminders, chase people that the ATEs staffing system shows but who sent no survey, and write back with follow-up questions. Managers have complained that the process is a burden. The September 2000 move to an Access database made entry menu-driven, but managers still key in their hours every month.",
  "change": "Send each manager a survey already filled in with last month's figures, ATEs staff numbers and system report counts, so they only confirm or fix what has changed.",
  "explanation": "The OPM team would load each RC's hours survey with last month's activity split and the current ATEs staff count, so managers confirm it or edit only the lines that changed. For the driver survey, the OPM team would take up its own standing offer for every RC: tie each driver to an existing standard report (deal counts and similar) that is sent to OPM automatically, so the manager no longer types those numbers. The database would list RCs that have staff in ATEs but no confirmed survey, which replaces finding them by hand. Afterwards managers spend a few minutes confirming, driver numbers arrive from reports where one exists, and the OPM team sends fewer reminders and queries.",
  "occurrences": [
    {
      "file": "corpus/farmer-d/logistics/1243.eml",
      "quote": "Attached please find the Hours Survey and Instructions for the month of June, \n2000."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/farmer-d/logistics/1084.eml",
      "quote": "Please select your RCs, \nand fill in the driver quantity for the requested driver"
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/farmer-d/logistics/1244.eml",
      "quote": "Attached please find the Activity Survey for the month of June, 2000."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/farmer-d/logistics/1180.eml",
      "quote": "Attached please find the Activity Survey for the month of May, 2000."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/farmer-d/logistics/1415.eml",
      "quote": "On Wednesday, September 27, 2000 a new Hours Survey will be distributed to \nyou and will be due for completion on Wednesday, October 4, 2000."
    }
  ],
  "evidence": [
    {
      "file": "corpus/farmer-d/logistics/1188.eml",
      "quote": "The deadline was Friday, 6/2, and unfortunately, very few of you \nresponded.  I understand how busy each of you are and you have expressed your \nconcerns on the process burdening you.",
      "note": "Most managers miss the deadline and call the survey a burden, so a senior manager has to chase them."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/farmer-d/logistics/923.eml",
      "quote": "ATEs shows that your team has one specialist for 1497 in January and \nFebruary.",
      "note": "The OPM team already compares ATEs staff numbers with the surveys by hand to find missing ones; the database could do this check itself."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/farmer-d/logistics/923.eml",
      "quote": "This lack of information prevents your expenses \nfrom being 100% allocated out to the commercial teams.",
      "note": "A missing survey holds up the cost allocation."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/farmer-d/logistics/1084.eml",
      "quote": "If your group currently generates a standard report that captures the \nsurveyed data, please send the report to me, and put me on your recipient \nlist beginning next month.  This will eliminate your need to fill out this \nsurvey every month.",
      "note": "The OPM team itself says a standard report can replace the driver survey. The offer is repeated each month, so uptake seems partial; the change is to set it up for every RC."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/farmer-d/logistics/1180.eml",
      "quote": "Please provide the number of Producer Services deals for the month of May \n(New vs. Existing)",
      "note": "The driver numbers are counts such as deals, which already exist in systems; OPM chases them one manager at a time."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/farmer-d/logistics/1243.eml",
      "quote": "If your hours have not changed from last month, please send us an email to \nindicate so.",
      "note": "Unchanged months already need only a short email, so the hours saving comes mainly from months with changes, where pre-filled lines avoid re-entering everything."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/farmer-d/logistics/1445.eml",
      "quote": "As a reminder, today is the deadline for completion of the OPM Survey.",
      "note": "Deadline reminders go out to the whole list."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/farmer-d/logistics/1447.eml",
      "quote": "One thing I still need from you is what \ncommercial teams your group was supporting overall ?",
      "note": "Follow-up questions after a survey is returned; carrying last month's commercial-team split forward would answer this one."
    }
  ],
  "ongoing": true,
  "stated_rate": {
    "count": 1,
    "per": "month",
    "file": "corpus/farmer-d/logistics/1244.eml",
    "quote": "will eliminate your need to fill out this survey every month"
  },
  "minutes": 400
}

{
  "name": "Monthly OPM hours and activity-driver surveys",
  "change": "Pre-fill each manager's hours survey from ATEs headcount and last month's split, and replace driver surveys with standard system reports, so managers only confirm changes.",
  "reason": "The mail shows most of the change was already in place (the Access hours survey rolled over FTEs and commercial teams and printed prior-month hours by activity, unchanged months needed only an email, and every driver survey already offered a standard report instead), so the minutes saved are not supported; two critics have already rejected the same work for this reason.",
  "research": "Find mail showing what still costs managers time in the Access survey after rollover existed, how many RCs actually switched to sending reports and why others did not, and how often OPM chases missing surveys; a proposal aimed only at that remaining gap (for example an automatic missing-survey list from ATEs) might hold up."
}

{
  "name": "Calpine daily gas nomination to HPL scheduler",
  "change": "Replace Calpine's daily phone call plus Word-document nomination with a standing nomination in HPL's system that rolls forward and is changed only by exception through electronic entry.",
  "reason": "Most of the minutes claimed come from steps the mail does not show happening daily: a phone call (mentioned in 4 of about 23 nominations), a scheduler confirmation reply (one undated internal Giron-to-Poorman note, not a reply to Calpine), and frequent no-change days that would make a standing nomination worthwhile (no evidence; monthly totals and REVISED resends show the volumes change).",
  "research": "Find scheduler replies to Ricky Archer's nominations, and nomination contents or comparisons that show how often Calpine's daily volumes actually repeat; also whether HPL had an electronic nomination entry Calpine could use."
}

{
  "name": "Monthly search of Houston books for Enron Canada (ECC) deals",
  "today": "Deals that should settle through Enron Canada (ECC) often land in Houston trading books, many put there automatically by EnronOnline. Before each month's NYMEX invoicing, Stacey Vallejo in Calgary settlements searches the Houston books, lists the deals she finds, and emails 6-8 Houston staff (Gossett, Giron, Keiser, Kelly, Baumbach, Dawson, McLaughlin and others) asking them to go through all their books and move ECC deals to the FT-US/CAND-ERMS book. Giron forwards each request to his 5-7 book administrators, who each search their own books. Invoicing for both ECC and ENA waits until this is done. EnronOnline already books TransCanada Energy and Dynegy Canada deals to ECC automatically, but other counterparties such as Duke and Aquila Canada are not covered, and deals booked as ENA with a Canadian counterparty do not show up as ECC deals, so some are still missed and a second round of requests follows.",
  "change": "Book deals with every ECC counterparty to FT-US/CAND-ERMS automatically and send a daily list of any that slip through, instead of a monthly search of all books.",
  "explanation": "EnronOnline would extend the rule it already has for TransCanada Energy and Dynegy Canada to every counterparty that ECC has a master agreement with (Duke Energy Marketing, Aquila Canada and others), so those deals are booked to FT-US/CAND-ERMS from the start. A saved Tagg query, like the calculation Giron already uses to find these deals, would run each night and email Stacey Vallejo and the book's administrator any deal with ECC or a listed Canadian counterparty that sits outside FT-US/CAND-ERMS. The administrator moves it the next morning. At NYMEX close there is no request to everyone to search their books, and invoicing can start on time.",
  "occurrences": [
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/550.eml",
      "quote": "Could you please tell everyone down there that books deals into Houston\nbooks, to make sure that there aren't any ECC deals with counterparties\nin these books."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/535.eml",
      "quote": "Just a quick request for you to go into all your books to make sure that \nthere are no ECC deals booked there."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/407.eml",
      "quote": "Could you please \nmake sure that there aren't any more deals with ECC and a third counterparty \nin this book as it messes up invoicing and settlement."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/360.eml",
      "quote": "Just a friendly reminder for you to please go through all your books to make \nsure\nthere aren't any deals between ECC and a third counterparty."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/292.eml",
      "quote": "Here is a list of deals that I know of that need to be flipped to the \nFT-US/CAND-ERMS book right away.  Please go through your books to see if \nthere are any deals that I might have missed."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/195.eml",
      "quote": "This is just a quick reminder for all of you to please go into all of your \nbooks and flip out all the deals that are supposed to settle with ECC and a \nthird counterparty  to the FT-US/CAND-ERMS book by the end of the day today."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/114.eml",
      "quote": "Here is a list of the deals that I've come across in the different books that \nstill need to be flipped"
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/108.eml",
      "quote": "What I'm \nrequesting is that you go through all your books and look for all deals with \nAquila\nCanada Corp."
    }
  ],
  "evidence": [
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/535.eml",
      "quote": "Invoicing for November should \nstart today, and both ECC and ENA are held back from invoicing until these \ndeals are fixed",
      "note": "Invoicing for both companies waits until every book has been searched and fixed."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/550.eml",
      "quote": "These are all EnronOnline deals so they\nwere put into this book automatically.",
      "note": "The wrong books come from automatic booking, so a booking rule addresses the cause."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/292.eml",
      "quote": "I've spoken to Jennifer Denny with EOL about getting a \nprogram set up for Duke deals similar to ones we have with TransCanada Energy \nand Dynegy Canada so they automatically get booked to settle with ECC, but I \ndon't think this has happened yet.",
      "note": "EnronOnline already books two counterparties to ECC automatically; the change extends this to the rest."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/195.eml",
      "quote": "Please take care of this if you have any to be flipped.",
      "note": "Giron passes each request on to his book administrators, who each search their books."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/360.eml",
      "quote": "Goss said you may have a calc set up to identify these deals.  Any chance I \ncould copy it?",
      "note": "A query that finds these deals already exists but is shared person to person; running it nightly for everyone replaces the manual searches."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/108.eml",
      "quote": "These deals would not have shown up when\nyou looked for deals to flip to the FT-US/CAND-ERMS book as they aren't in\nTAGG as ECC deals.  I have a feeling that there are lots of deals like this in\nTAGG, but I just don't know where.",
      "note": "Searching by hand misses deals booked as ENA with a Canadian counterparty, which leads to a second round; a counterparty-based rule and report would catch them."
    },
    {
      "file": "corpus/giron-d/sent/108.eml",
      "quote": "I'm missing at least 10 deals from the April 2001 Nymex invoice",
      "note": "Misses still affect the invoices."
    }
  ],
  "ongoing": true,
  "stated_rate": null,
  "minutes": 260
}

