{
  "name": "Monthly Investor Relations volumetric explanations",
  "change": "Have the Statistical Database flag the +/-10% variances, show EOL and counterparty drivers, pre-fill last month's explanation, and collect the controllers' explanations in the database instead of by email.",
  "reason": "The change depends on things the mail does not show: that the Statistical Database holds EOL and counterparty detail, and that it does not already show the variances. The minutes are also inflated: 11 controllers' work is costed from one controller's two-line reply, and 11 readings are counted for a verifier who was copied only because one controller chose to copy him.",
  "research": "Look for mail showing what the Statistical Database contains (variance columns, EOL or counterparty breakdowns), replies from controllers other than Baumbach, and other months' requests, and use them to show how long the explanations take and whether they repeat; then cost only the steps the change really removes."
}

